   "headline": "KOSPI rebounds 1.39% after a volatile session, with foreign outflows continuing",
   "when": "Thu 19 Nov · Seoul close",
   "what": "KOSPI closed at 5,137.89 after trading lower at midday. Samsung Electronics rose 1.13% and SK hynix 3.41%; both had been down about 2% earlier. Kosdaq gained 3.32%. Foreign investors sold a net 31 trillion won of Korean shares from October to Wednesday, about 24 trillion of it chips. The won ended at 1,330 per dollar. Separately, Korea's annual exports passed $1 trillion for the first time.",
